  "page_text": "                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n       6  Technical data                                                          \n                                                                                  \n       It is important to observe the technical data during installation, operation and maintenance.\n       Inform personnel about the technical data.                                 \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n       6.1 Technical data                                                         \n                                                                                  \n       The LKH pump is a highly efficient and econominal centrifugal pump, which meets the requirements of sanitary and gentle\n       product treatment and chemical resistance. LKH Prime is available in the sizes specified on the declaration of conformity\n       chapter 1. The instruction manual is part of the delivery. Read the instructions carefully. The pump is very heavy. Alfa Laval\n       recommends the use of a lifting crane when handling the pump.              \n       DDDaaatttaaa                                                               \n                                                                                  \n       Max. inlet pressure       500 kPa (5 bar) (72.5 psi )                      \n       Temperature range         -10oC to +140oC (EPDM) (14 to 284oF )            \n       Max. speed:               3600 rpm                                         \n       Min. speed, pumping product (no air): 900RPM                               \n       Min. speed, releasing air: 2800RPM (full speed 2 poled motor, 50Hz)        \n       MMMaaattteeerrriiiaaalllsss                                                \n                                                                                  \n       Product wetted steel parts AISI 316L                                       \n       Other steel parts         Stainless steel                                  \n       Finish                    Standard blasted                                 \n       Product wetted seals      EPDM (standard)                                  \n       Other O-rings             EPDM (standard)                                  \n       Alternative seals         Nitrile (NBR) and fluorinated rubber (FPM)       \n       SSShhhaaafffttt ssseeeaaalll                                               \n                                                                                  \n       Seal types                External single or double mechanical seal        \n       Max. temperature flush medium 70oC                                         \n       Max. water pressure (DMS) Normally atmospheric (max. 5 bar) (max. 72.5 psi)\n       Water consumption (double mechanical seal) 0.25-0.5 l/min. (0.07-0.13 gl ) \n       Material, stationary seal ring Acid-resistant steel with sealing surface of silicon carbide\n       Material, rotating seal ring Carbon (standard) or silicon carbide          \n       Material, O-rings         EPDM (standard)                                  \n       Alternative material, O-rings Nitrile (NBR) and fluorinated rubber (FPM).  \n       Air release time (no medium supply) Max 15 min                             \n       NNNOOOTTTEEE: If running SiC/SiC single seal, the static seal face must be marked “LKH Prime”.\n       MMMoootttooorrr                                                            \n       Foot-flanged motor according to IEC metric or NEMA standard, 2 poles = 3000/3600 rpm. at 50/60 Hz IP55, insulation class F\n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n       For further information, see PD sheet.                                     \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n       42                                                                         ",
